# Docs

## CLI reference

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `creestal new <name>` | Scaffold a new site |
| `creestal build` | Build the site into `out/` |
| `creestal serve` | Serve `out/` locally with live-reload |
| `creestal serve --port 8080` | Serve on a custom port |

## Layouts

A layout is an HTML file in `layouts/`. It wraps every page that references it.

The page's rendered content is available as `page.content`:

```jinja
<main>{{ page.content }}</main>
```

Open `layouts/base.html` to see this in action.

## Partials

A partial is an HTML file in `partials/`. Include partials directly from your layout:

```jinja
{% include "header.html" %}
```

Included partials can access the same render context (`page`, `site`, and `active_page`) as the parent template.

## Active page

Views also receive `active_page`, which is the current page source path without extension (for example: `index`, `about`, `blog/first-post`).

Use `is_active(current, value)` to conditionally return any string value.

```jinja
<a class="{{ is_active("docs", "is-active") }}" href="/docs">Docs</a>
```

## Breadcrumbs

The `site` context includes page-aware breadcrumbs at `site.breadcrumbs`.

```jinja
{% if site.breadcrumbs|length > 1 %}
	<ol class="breadcrumb">
		{% for crumb in site.breadcrumbs %}
			{% if crumb.output_path == page.output_path %}
				<li class="breadcrumb-item"><span>{{ crumb.title }}</span></li>
			{% else %}
				<li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="{{ crumb.url }}">{{ crumb.title }}</a></li>
			{% endif %}
		{% endfor %}
	</ol>
{% endif %}
```

## Config reference

`config.yml` at the root of your site:

```yaml
site: <%= @ctx.app_name %>          # site title
source: <%= @ctx.source %>          # directory containing pages/, layouts/, etc.
output: out                         # where the built site is written
default_layout: base                # layout used when none is specified in frontmatter
```

## Adding pages

Drop a Markdown file anywhere inside `pages/`. The output path mirrors the source path:

```
pages/blog/my-post.md  →  out/blog/my-post.html
```

→ Continue to [Blog → First Post](/blog/first-post)
